.Dd July 5, 2026
.Dt XTC_FREE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_free
.Nd free a heap buffer libxtc handed the caller to own
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_free "void *p"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn xtc_free
releases a heap buffer that a libxtc call allocated and handed to the
caller to own.
Several APIs return caller-owned buffers and document that they must be
released with
.Fn xtc_free :
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
the message buffer from
.Xr xtc_recv 3 ,
.Fn xtc_recv_match ,
and
.Fn xtc_recv_correlate ;
.It
the frame from
.Fn xtc_net_recv_frame ;
.It
the reply buffer from
.Fn xtc_osproc_call
and
.Fn xtc_svr_call .
.El
.Pp
These buffers are allocated by libxtc's own allocator, which is not
necessarily the C library
.Xr malloc 3 Ns / Ns Xr free 3 ,
so they must be released through
.Fn xtc_free
rather than plain
.Xr free 3 .
Passing
.Dv NULL
is a no-op.
.Fn xtc_free
is safe to call from any thread.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_free
returns no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_net 3 ,
.Xr xtc_osproc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_svr 3
